


FRACTAL(1)          FGX Programmer's Manual            FRACTAL(1)



NAME
     fractal - interactive fractal explorer (SHR 320x200x16)

SYNOPSIS
     fractal [ --draw | --rainbow | --sum ]

DESCRIPTION
     Fractal renders escape-time fractals on the Super Hi-Res
     320x200 16-color screen and lets you explore them with a
     crosshair.  Rendering is progressive: a chunky preview of
     the whole image appears almost immediately and sharpens in
     place.  All keys work while a render is still painting.

     The compute engine is Q9 fixed point driven by a quarter-
     square multiply table (no hardware multiply), with interior
     shortcuts (cardioid/bulb tests, Brent cycle detection) that
     are bit-exact against a host reference oracle.

KEYS
     arrows       move the crosshair 1 pixel (summons it if
                  hidden; works during rendering)
     ctrl-arrows  move 8 pixels (HJKL also work)
     enter        zoom 2x centered on the crosshair.  Zoom is
                  capped at two steps by the Q9 step size.
     f            cycle fractal type: Mandelbrot, Tricorn,
                  Burning Ship, cubic Multibrot
     j            render the Julia set of the point under the
                  crosshair (Mandelbrot only); esc returns to
                  the saved Mandelbrot view
     p            cycle palettes: grey-red, grey, rainbow, fire,
                  ice, and the user palette when present.  The
                  finished image recolors instantly.
     h, ?         pop up the key summary
     esc          back out of a Julia set, otherwise exit
     q            quit from anywhere

OPTIONS
     --draw       explorer mode (the default)
     --rainbow    start with the rainbow palette and classic
                  mod-15 color cycling
     --sum        print the compute oracle checksum (testing)

FILES
     /etc/fractal.pal    optional user palette: 16 whitespace-
                         separated hex RGB12 values, e.g.
                         000 111 222 ... F00.  Entry 0 is the
                         set interior (usually black).  Joins
                         the p cycle when valid.
     /lib/fonts/default.fnt   console font, used by the help box

NOTES
     Fractal runs only on the physical console.  The Super
     Hi-Res screen is the machine and there is exactly one of
     it, so there is no per-terminal framebuffer to follow a
     session onto; started from a pty or a virtual console it
     prints a diagnostic and exits rather than paint over a
     display its user cannot see.  It asks /dev/tty which line
     it is on, so redirecting its input or output does not
     change the answer.  The checksum options below are exempt:
     they touch no screen.

     Deeper zoom awaits a wider multiply engine; two zoom steps
     exhaust the Q9 pixel step.  Julia sets, the Burning Ship,
     and off-axis zooms compute all 200 rows; axis-symmetric
     views mirror and render nearly twice as fast.

BUGS
     The 16-palette-per-scanline hardware caps on-screen colors
     at 16; the parked 3200-color engine may return someday.



